   178	## §5 — Per-loop discipline
   179	
   180	Inside any Chat-Mode loop slice (Ideation / Preparation when not skipped / mini Planning / mini
   181	Execution):
   182	
   183	- **DISCUSSION is forced user-driven**, regardless of the resolved `discuss.mode`. The leader
   184	  proposes (research-backed); the user decides via `AskUserQuestion`. This is the discuss-first
   185	  Chat-Mode property; it does not override `discuss.mode` in settings (settings still resolve to
   186	  `"user"` everywhere in the Chat defaults), but it is documented here so a future settings change
   187	  cannot accidentally regress it.
   188	- **Three mode-specific gates within a loop** still apply (per `orchestration/SKILL.md §
   189	  Mode-specific gates within a loop`): after DISCUSSION → confirm delegation prompt; after
   190	  EVALUATION → discuss findings and remediation; at ITER/EXIT → confirm exit.
   191	- **Iteration cap is 2** for Ideation / Planning / Execution (Auto's default is 3). The narrower
   192	  budget reflects Chat's per-task scope: a user-typed task that needs three iterations is a signal
   193	  to reframe or split, not iterate further.
   194	- **Evaluation always runs.** `evaluate.mode: always` across all loops in Chat.
   195	- **MEMORIZATION runs every loop with the §4 narrowed PASS path.**
   196	- **Fresh subagent context per slice.** Every leader / executor / evaluator spawn pastes its
   197	  context inline — no cross-task subagent memory. The manager is the only durable cross-task
   198	  agent. Governance: `delegation/SKILL.md § Inline-Paste Rule` (the discipline) and Principle 1
   199	  (the underlying behavioral law — "no action without thinking it through first"; iter1's Principle
   200	  4 citation was a wrong-number reference, corrected per §8 L-P1/L-C2/L-U1 of the Idea doc for
   201	  this redesign).
   202	- **Mistake-stage moment-of-capture.** Every correction the manager or any subagent identifies in
   203	  a Chat per-task slice is staged immediately at
   204	  `sessions/.../{loop}/staging/decisions/{slug}.md` with `mistake-candidate: true`, per
   205	  `mistake/SKILL.md § P2`. This is the explicit exception to §4's "Steps 6–7 skipped" narrowing
   206	  — the moment-of-capture is governed by the `mistake` skill, not by `memorization/SKILL.md`.
   207	
